{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00488",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.58,
      "end_seconds": 5.72,
      "duration_seconds": 5.14,
      "text": "Hi, doctor, I brought my bag, is it fine to leave it here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.4,
      "end_seconds": 10.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "Alright, of course, put it down anywhere. So, how can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.59,
      "end_seconds": 25.47,
      "duration_seconds": 13.88,
      "text": "Well, I've been having pain in my lower back. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.37,
      "end_seconds": 28.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "How long have you had it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 29.68,
      "end_seconds": 32.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "It's been about two weeks, I'm fairly sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.65,
      "end_seconds": 36.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "And what do you do to cope with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.79,
      "end_seconds": 42.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.84,
      "text": "It settles a little with lying flat and a hot water bag."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.19,
      "end_seconds": 44.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "How often does it happen?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.88,
      "end_seconds": 49.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "Honestly, a couple of times a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.49,
      "end_seconds": 53.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "How would you describe it, mild, moderate, severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.3,
      "end_seconds": 71.84,
      "duration_seconds": 16.54,
      "text": "I'd say mild. Oh, uh, and stiffness. That's been about the same, four weeks. With stiffness, stretching helps a bit. There's pain going into the buttock as well. I, I did have difficulty bending forward at one point, but that's gone now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.54,
      "end_seconds": 79.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "Right, do you have everything you need to get home alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.19,
      "end_seconds": 94.02,
      "duration_seconds": 12.83,
      "text": "Yes, I've got my transport sorted. It's a bit of a trek, but I'm used to the journey by now, and I brought something to read for the wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.35,
      "end_seconds": 98.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Any weakness in the legs or numbness in the legs at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.09,
      "end_seconds": 104.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "No. None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.23,
      "end_seconds": 108.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "Any fever, weight loss or numbness around the groin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.2,
      "end_seconds": 114.84,
      "duration_seconds": 5.64,
      "text": "Hmm, I haven't had fever, weight loss or numbness around the groin, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.29,
      "end_seconds": 119.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "How about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.49,
      "end_seconds": 123.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "Well, no, nothing with my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.8,
      "end_seconds": 124.79,
      "duration_seconds": 0.99,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.1,
      "end_seconds": 132.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "No, um, never had any surgery."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.69,
      "end_seconds": 135.17,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.96,
      "end_seconds": 139.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "A beer or two most evenings, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.9,
      "end_seconds": 141.64,
      "duration_seconds": 0.74,
      "text": "Any smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.63,
      "end_seconds": 145.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "I smoke, yes, around five a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.32,
      "end_seconds": 149.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "What medicines are you taking at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.51,
      "end_seconds": 167.67,
      "duration_seconds": 13.16,
      "text": "It's ramipril, 5 milligrams, every morning for my blood pressure. I took the morning off to come in today. I take diclofenac, 50 milligrams, when needed for the joint pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 168.18,
      "end_seconds": 172.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 100 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.08,
      "end_seconds": 176.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "Okay. Have you got the newest prescription or the box with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 177.94,
      "end_seconds": 180.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "No, I left it at home."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.93,
      "end_seconds": 189.25,
      "duration_seconds": 7.32,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for? These questions might sound routine, but they matter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 190.05,
      "end_seconds": 196.27,
      "duration_seconds": 6.22,
      "text": "I have high blood pressure. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.58,
      "end_seconds": 197.28,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Mm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 198.12,
      "end_seconds": 202.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "I have arthritis in my knees, for five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.14,
      "end_seconds": 212.2,
      "duration_seconds": 9.06,
      "text": "Mm. Yes, I can see the arthritis in my knees in your file as well. Okay, anyone in the family with similar problems or other conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 213.72,
      "end_seconds": 215.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "My father had a stroke."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.16,
      "end_seconds": 220.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "Sorry, I'm just writing a few notes, bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.83,
      "end_seconds": 224.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "I mean, no problem, take your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.69,
      "end_seconds": 230.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "Alright, do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.6,
      "end_seconds": 233.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "Not that I know, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.68,
      "end_seconds": 237.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Did you manage to eat before coming?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.38,
      "end_seconds": 241.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "Yes, I had something small this morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 242.26,
      "end_seconds": 250.32,
      "duration_seconds": 8.06,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Heart rate 80, respiratory rate 16, oxygen saturation is 99 percent. BP is 113 over 82, temperature 36.6."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.5,
      "end_seconds": 252.2,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.73,
      "end_seconds": 256.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "Can I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.14,
      "end_seconds": 258.92,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "Let me check your reflexes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.44,
      "end_seconds": 281.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "Straight leg raise is negative on both sides and power in the legs is normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.67,
      "end_seconds": 286.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "A little pressure here, tell me if it's tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.39,
      "end_seconds": 305.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.27,
      "text": "There's tenderness over the muscles on the right of the lower back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 306.43,
      "end_seconds": 307.13,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Hm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.38,
      "end_seconds": 326.84,
      "duration_seconds": 17.46,
      "text": "That's fine, you can get dressed. I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 327.54,
      "end_seconds": 330.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "Thank you, uh, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 333.78,
      "end_seconds": 342.64,
      "duration_seconds": 8.86,
      "text": "Okay, so my impression is this: I think we're dealing with mechanical low back pain at this stage. I'd also keep a disc problem in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 343.89,
      "end_seconds": 347.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "Okay, so should I be worried about this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 347.82,
      "end_seconds": 370.33,
      "duration_seconds": 22.51,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's mechanical low back pain, and we'll know more once the an MRI of the lumbar spine is back. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had pain in your lower back for about two weeks, mild, and no weight loss or numbness around the groin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 370.72,
      "end_seconds": 373.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Exactly, that's what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 374.21,
      "end_seconds": 403.42,
      "duration_seconds": 29.21,
      "text": "Let's get an MRI of the lumbar spine, for persistent back pain. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more. I'm going to order an X-ray of the lower back, for back pain. I'm prescribing thiocolchicoside, 4 milligrams, twice a day, for five days. That's for muscle spasm. Every hour, get up and stretch if you're at a desk. Staying gently active heals back pain faster than bed rest, so keep moving."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 404.73,
      "end_seconds": 411.26,
      "duration_seconds": 6.53,
      "text": "Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day. We'll refer you to physiotherapy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 412.8,
      "end_seconds": 414.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "Sure, where do I go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 416.35,
      "end_seconds": 423.89,
      "duration_seconds": 7.54,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 425.42,
      "end_seconds": 426.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.28,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 428.23,
      "end_seconds": 436.75,
      "duration_seconds": 8.52,
      "text": "If you get numbness in the groin or lose bladder control, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 438.31,
      "end_seconds": 440.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Yes, you know, I'll do that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 441.61,
      "end_seconds": 443.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Let's review you in two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 445.37,
      "end_seconds": 448.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "Sure, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 450.36,
      "end_seconds": 456.36,
      "duration_seconds": 6.0,
      "text": "I want to be sure we're on the same page. How would you describe the plan?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 457.76,
      "end_seconds": 465.12,
      "duration_seconds": 7.36,
      "text": "So, I take the thiocolchicoside, 4 milligrams, twice a day and come back in two weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0068",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 465.64,
      "end_seconds": 469.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0069",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 471.14,
      "end_seconds": 474.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "Okay, thank you. I'll get started on all of that."
    }
  ]
}